# Jetnity Progress Persistence – Always Apply

`docs/PROJECT_PROGRESS_PERSISTENCE_POLICY.md` is mandatory.

For Foundation D and every Jetnity work block:

- Do not keep important progress only in agent/session/chat context.
- Persist product decisions, implementation milestones, blockers, review findings, test/CI/Preview state, DB/Production boundaries, risks, pending approvals and the exact next step in the repository.
- Keep `docs/ACTIVE_WORK_STATUS.md` current during active work.
- Before pausing, handing off, closing an agent, or reporting a major milestone, update the active work status and affected durable docs.
- A new agent must read the current handoff, roadmap, progress-persistence policy, merge-approval policy, active PR/branch, `docs/ACTIVE_WORK_STATUS.md`, current task and newer amendments before continuing.
- Never claim progress, tests, Preview, Production or completion that was not verified.
- Never merge without explicit current Product Owner approval.

Goal: no relevant Jetnity progress may be lost when a chat, agent or session changes.
